title: Frame
description: A framed container for grouping related information.
---

<ComponentPreview name="p-frame-1" />

## Installation

<InstallCommand pnpm="pnpm add @coss-sv/ui" shadcnSvelte="pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/frame.json" />

## Usage

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import {
    Frame,
    FrameDescription,
    FrameFooter,
    FrameHeader,
    FramePanel,
    FrameTitle,
  } from "@coss-sv/ui/components/ui/frame";
</script>

<Frame>
  <FrameHeader>
    <FrameTitle>Title</FrameTitle>
    <FrameDescription>Description</FrameDescription>
  </FrameHeader>
  <FramePanel>Content</FramePanel>
  <FrameFooter>Footer</FrameFooter>
</Frame>
```

## API Reference

### Frame

The main container for grouping related information. It accepts native `div` attributes, a bindable
`ref`, snippets, and `class`.

### FramePanel

A panel container for frame content. It accepts native `div` attributes.

```svelte
<FramePanel>Content</FramePanel>
```

### FrameHeader

The semantic header section for a frame.

```svelte
<FrameHeader>
  <FrameTitle>Title</FrameTitle>
  <FrameDescription>Description</FrameDescription>
</FrameHeader>
```

### FrameTitle

The frame heading text.

```svelte
<FrameTitle>Title</FrameTitle>
```

### FrameDescription

The supporting text for a frame header.

```svelte
<FrameDescription>Description</FrameDescription>
```

### FrameFooter

The semantic footer section for a frame.

```svelte
<FrameFooter>Footer</FrameFooter>
```

## Examples

### Separated Panels

By default, multiple panels are separated with spacing between them.

